course: dictionary
lesson: 7333
title: One word, many planners
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A planner is someone who plans things, like a wedding planner who organises a wedding, or a town planner who decides where new roads and buildings may go. A planner can also be a thing: a book, diary or app where you write down plans and dates.
explain: Context tells you which meaning fits. «The teacher noticed, his friend got in trouble too, and Max's planner came home to be signed.» Max's planner is something that can be signed and taken home, so it is the diary he writes in, not a person.
explain: Two words together often give the meaning. A homework planner is a diary where you write down tasks, and a teacher or parent signs it to show they have seen it. Always check: when you put your meaning into the sentence, does it still make sense?
fact: A planner can be a person who plans, such as a wedding planner or a town planner.
fact: A planner can also be a book, diary or app for writing down plans and dates.
fact: «Homework planner» means a diary where pupils write down their homework tasks.
fact: In the UK, a town planner works for the council, deciding where new buildings and roads may go.
fact: «Planner» is a noun, and its plural is planners.
exercise: «The teacher signed Max's planner after he wrote his tasks in it.» What is the planner here? | *A diary where he wrote his tasks | A map of the town | A person who plans weddings | A council worker who plans roads
exercise: A wedding planner helps a couple get married. What does a wedding planner do? | *Organises weddings | Writes books about trees | Signs homework diaries | Drives the school bus
exercise: Which phrase means a diary where pupils write down homework? | Wedding planner | *Homework planner | Good planner | Town planner
test: Mum says, «Your planner needs signing tonight.» What does planner mean here? | A wedding planner | *A diary where you write down tasks | A town planner from the council | A computer game
test: Which kind of planner decides where new roads and buildings may go? | A planner app for birthdays | *A town planner | A homework planner | A wedding planner
exam: In «She wrote a note in his planner, and Mum and Dad had to sign it.» what is his planner? | A kind of bird | *A book or diary where he writes plans and dates | A person who plans his holidays | A council office
